IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `clpa-dates`
IMPORT `clpa-claims`

-- Choice of Law (Limitation Periods) Act 1994 (WA) -- worked cases for the questions of the person bringing a claim.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Expected values were written by hand
-- from the text before the file was run; none was copied from the encoding's output. All facts are HYPOTHETICAL.
--
-- Sourced from the Western Australian Legislation website, State of Western Australia, CC BY 4.0 (SOURCE-LICENSE.md).
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Short names for the facts and the answers used below`

`7 Nov 2026` MEANS `the calendar date` 7 11 2026
`26 May 1994` MEANS `the calendar date` 26 5 1994
`27 May 1994` MEANS `the calendar date` 27 5 1994
`1 Jun 1993` MEANS `the calendar date` 1 6 1993
`31 Dec 1999` MEANS `the calendar date` 31 12 1999
`1 Jan 2000` MEANS `the calendar date` 1 1 2000
`15 Feb 2020` MEANS `the calendar date` 15 2 2020
`1 Mar 2020` MEANS `the calendar date` 1 3 2020
`10 Jun 2020` MEANS `the calendar date` 10 6 2020
`7 Nov 2022` MEANS `the calendar date` 7 11 2022
`28 Feb 2023` MEANS `the calendar date` 28 2 2023
`1 Mar 2023` MEANS `the calendar date` 1 3 2023
`2 Mar 2023` MEANS `the calendar date` 2 3 2023
`29 Feb 2024` MEANS `the calendar date` 29 2 2024
`28 Feb 2027` MEANS `the calendar date` 28 2 2027
`1 Mar 2027` MEANS `the calendar date` 1 3 2027

`another State` MEANS `the law of another Australian State`
`a Territory` MEANS `the law of an Australian Territory`
`NZ` MEANS `the law of New Zealand`
`WA law` MEANS `the law of Western Australia`
`a foreign country` MEANS `the law of a country other than Australia or New Zealand`
`WA court` MEANS `a court of Western Australia`
`WA arbitrator` MEANS `an arbitrator, in an arbitration held in Western Australia`
`outside WA` MEANS `a court or arbitrator outside Western Australia`

`APPLIES` MEANS `yes: the Act applies to these proceedings (s 3), even if the cause of action arose before 27 May 1994 (s 3(1))`
`TOO EARLY` MEANS `no: the proceedings were instituted before 27 May 1994 (s 3(1), the text's no)`
`NZ UNDECLARED` MEANS `no: New Zealand law governs the claim and no proclamation has declared that the Act applies in relation to New Zealand (s 3(2), the text's no)`
`NZ BEFORE DECLARATION` MEANS `no: New Zealand law governs the claim and the proceedings were instituted before the declaration for New Zealand was made (s 3(3), the text's no)`

`THAT PLACE'S LIMITATION LAW` MEANS `the limitation law of the place whose law governs the claim applies to it, as part of that place's substantive law (s 5)`
`S5 NOT UNDER THIS ACT` MEANS `not under this Act: it does not apply to these proceedings (s 3, the text's no)`
`S5 NOT A WA COURT` MEANS `s 5 does not apply: the claim is not before a court or arbitrator of Western Australia (the text's no: its "if" fails); this Act does not say which time limit applies`
`S5 NOT ANOTHER PLACE` MEANS `s 5 does not apply: the claim is not governed by the law of another State, a Territory or New Zealand (the text's no: its "if" fails); this Act does not say which time limit applies`

`IN TIME` MEANS `in time: you commenced on or before the last day the limitation law of the governing place allows (s 5)`
`STILL IN TIME` MEANS `still in time: you have not commenced, and the last day the limitation law of the governing place allows has not passed (s 5)`
`OUT OF TIME` MEANS `out of time under the limitation law of the governing place (s 5): only a discretion that law gives the court can help (see s 6)`
`NO TIME LIMIT FROM THIS ACT` MEANS `this Act does not make another place's time limit apply on these facts (s 3 or s 5, the text's no)`

`FAVOUR` MEANS `as the courts of that place do in comparable cases, and on these facts they would exercise it in your favour (s 6)`
`NOT FAVOUR` MEANS `as the courts of that place do in comparable cases, and on these facts they would not exercise it in your favour (s 6)`
`NOT PRACTICABLE` MEANS `s 6 asks the court to follow that place's courts only as far as practicable; here it is not practicable, and s 6 says no more (NOTHING-kind)`
`NO DISCRETION` MEANS `s 6 does not arise: that limitation law gives the court no discretion that you have asked it to exercise (the text's no: its "where" fails)`
`S6 NOT WA OR NOT ANOTHER PLACE` MEANS `s 6 does not arise: not a court or arbitrator of Western Australia, or not the limitation law of another State, a Territory or New Zealand (the text's no: its "where" fails)`
`S6 NOT UNDER THIS ACT` MEANS `s 6 does not arise under this Act: it does not apply to these proceedings (s 3, the text's no)`

§ `s 3 -- does this Act apply to my proceedings`

-- Instituted on the commencement day itself: not "before the commencement", so the Act applies (edge).
#ASSERT `s 3 -- does this Act apply to my proceedings` `another State` TRUE `27 May 1994` `7 Nov 2026` FALSE `1 Jan 2000` EQUALS `APPLIES`
-- Instituted the day before commencement (edge).
#ASSERT `s 3 -- does this Act apply to my proceedings` `another State` TRUE `26 May 1994` `7 Nov 2026` FALSE `1 Jan 2000` EQUALS `TOO EARLY`
-- Instituted in 1993, foreign law: s 3(1) first.
#ASSERT `s 3 -- does this Act apply to my proceedings` `a foreign country` TRUE `1 Jun 1993` `7 Nov 2026` FALSE `1 Jan 2000` EQUALS `TOO EARLY`
-- Not yet instituted: they will be instituted today or later, so the Act applies (a cause of action from before 1994 is no bar, s 3(1)).
#ASSERT `s 3 -- does this Act apply to my proceedings` `another State` FALSE `1 Jun 1993` `7 Nov 2026` FALSE `1 Jan 2000` EQUALS `APPLIES`
-- A Territory, instituted in 2020.
#ASSERT `s 3 -- does this Act apply to my proceedings` `a Territory` TRUE `10 Jun 2020` `7 Nov 2026` FALSE `1 Jan 2000` EQUALS `APPLIES`
-- WA law governs: s 3 does not exclude the proceedings (s 5 then does not reach them; see below).
#ASSERT `s 3 -- does this Act apply to my proceedings` `WA law` TRUE `10 Jun 2020` `7 Nov 2026` FALSE `1 Jan 2000` EQUALS `APPLIES`
-- New Zealand, no declaration: s 3(2).
#ASSERT `s 3 -- does this Act apply to my proceedings` `NZ` TRUE `10 Jun 2020` `7 Nov 2026` FALSE `1 Jan 2000` EQUALS `NZ UNDECLARED`
#ASSERT `s 3 -- does this Act apply to my proceedings` `NZ` FALSE `10 Jun 2020` `7 Nov 2026` FALSE `1 Jan 2000` EQUALS `NZ UNDECLARED`
-- New Zealand, declared 1 January 2000; instituted the day before (s 3(3)) and on the day (edge).
#ASSERT `s 3 -- does this Act apply to my proceedings` `NZ` TRUE `31 Dec 1999` `7 Nov 2026` TRUE `1 Jan 2000` EQUALS `NZ BEFORE DECLARATION`
#ASSERT `s 3 -- does this Act apply to my proceedings` `NZ` TRUE `1 Jan 2000` `7 Nov 2026` TRUE `1 Jan 2000` EQUALS `APPLIES`
-- New Zealand, declared, not yet instituted.
#ASSERT `s 3 -- does this Act apply to my proceedings` `NZ` FALSE `1 Jun 1993` `7 Nov 2026` TRUE `1 Jan 2000` EQUALS `APPLIES`
-- New Zealand declared by the commencement proclamation itself (27 May 1994), instituted 26 May 1994: s 3(1) is answered first.
#ASSERT `s 3 -- does this Act apply to my proceedings` `NZ` TRUE `26 May 1994` `7 Nov 2026` TRUE `27 May 1994` EQUALS `TOO EARLY`
-- The same declaration, instituted on 27 May 1994.
#ASSERT `s 3 -- does this Act apply to my proceedings` `NZ` TRUE `27 May 1994` `7 Nov 2026` TRUE `27 May 1994` EQUALS `APPLIES`
-- The declaration date is not used where New Zealand law does not govern.
#ASSERT `s 3 -- does this Act apply to my proceedings` `another State` TRUE `31 Dec 1999` `7 Nov 2026` TRUE `1 Jan 2000` EQUALS `APPLIES`

§ `s 4 -- is it a limitation law`

#ASSERT `s 4 -- is it a limitation law` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 4 -- is it a limitation law` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 4 -- is it a limitation law` FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 4 -- is it a limitation law` FALSE FALSE)

§ `s 5 -- whose time limit applies to my claim`

-- A WA court, another State's law, instituted 2020.
#ASSERT `s 5 -- whose time limit applies to my claim` `WA court` `another State` TRUE `10 Jun 2020` `7 Nov 2026` FALSE `1 Jan 2000` EQUALS `THAT PLACE'S LIMITATION LAW`
-- An arbitrator in WA ("court includes arbitrator"), a Territory's law, not yet commenced.
#ASSERT `s 5 -- whose time limit applies to my claim` `WA arbitrator` `a Territory` FALSE `10 Jun 2020` `7 Nov 2026` FALSE `1 Jan 2000` EQUALS `THAT PLACE'S LIMITATION LAW`
-- New Zealand law, declared, instituted after the declaration.
#ASSERT `s 5 -- whose time limit applies to my claim` `WA court` `NZ` TRUE `10 Jun 2020` `7 Nov 2026` TRUE `1 Jan 2000` EQUALS `THAT PLACE'S LIMITATION LAW`
-- New Zealand law, no declaration.
#ASSERT `s 5 -- whose time limit applies to my claim` `WA court` `NZ` TRUE `10 Jun 2020` `7 Nov 2026` FALSE `1 Jan 2000` EQUALS `S5 NOT UNDER THIS ACT`
-- Instituted before 27 May 1994.
#ASSERT `s 5 -- whose time limit applies to my claim` `WA court` `another State` TRUE `1 Jun 1993` `7 Nov 2026` FALSE `1 Jan 2000` EQUALS `S5 NOT UNDER THIS ACT`
-- Instituted before 27 May 1994 and heard outside WA: s 3 is answered first.
#ASSERT `s 5 -- whose time limit applies to my claim` `outside WA` `another State` TRUE `1 Jun 1993` `7 Nov 2026` FALSE `1 Jan 2000` EQUALS `S5 NOT UNDER THIS ACT`
-- Heard outside WA.
#ASSERT `s 5 -- whose time limit applies to my claim` `outside WA` `another State` TRUE `10 Jun 2020` `7 Nov 2026` FALSE `1 Jan 2000` EQUALS `S5 NOT A WA COURT`
-- WA law governs; a foreign country's law governs.
#ASSERT `s 5 -- whose time limit applies to my claim` `WA court` `WA law` TRUE `10 Jun 2020` `7 Nov 2026` FALSE `1 Jan 2000` EQUALS `S5 NOT ANOTHER PLACE`
#ASSERT `s 5 -- whose time limit applies to my claim` `WA court` `a foreign country` TRUE `10 Jun 2020` `7 Nov 2026` FALSE `1 Jan 2000` EQUALS `S5 NOT ANOTHER PLACE`
-- Heard outside WA and a foreign law: the forum is answered first.
#ASSERT `s 5 -- whose time limit applies to my claim` `outside WA` `a foreign country` TRUE `10 Jun 2020` `7 Nov 2026` FALSE `1 Jan 2000` EQUALS `S5 NOT A WA COURT`

§ `s 5 -- am I in time`

-- The regulative rule on its own: 1095 days allowed; commencing on day 0, day 1095 (the last day) and day 1096.
#ASSERT `s 5 -- commencing on this day is in time` 1095 0
#ASSERT `s 5 -- commencing on this day is in time` 1095 1095
#ASSERT NOT (`s 5 -- commencing on this day is in time` 1095 1096)

-- Time began 1 March 2020; the governing law's last day is 1 March 2023 (1095 days on: 2020-03-01 to 2023-03-01 crosses no 29 February).
-- Commenced on the last day (edge), the day before, and the day after.
#ASSERT `s 5 -- am I in time` `WA court` `another State` TRUE `1 Mar 2023` `7 Nov 2026` FALSE `1 Jan 2000` `1 Mar 2020` `1 Mar 2023` EQUALS `IN TIME`
#ASSERT `s 5 -- am I in time` `WA court` `another State` TRUE `28 Feb 2023` `7 Nov 2026` FALSE `1 Jan 2000` `1 Mar 2020` `1 Mar 2023` EQUALS `IN TIME`
#ASSERT `s 5 -- am I in time` `WA court` `another State` TRUE `2 Mar 2023` `7 Nov 2026` FALSE `1 Jan 2000` `1 Mar 2020` `1 Mar 2023` EQUALS `OUT OF TIME`
-- Commenced on the day time began, and before it.
#ASSERT `s 5 -- am I in time` `WA court` `another State` TRUE `1 Mar 2020` `7 Nov 2026` FALSE `1 Jan 2000` `1 Mar 2020` `1 Mar 2023` EQUALS `IN TIME`
#ASSERT `s 5 -- am I in time` `WA court` `another State` TRUE `15 Feb 2020` `7 Nov 2026` FALSE `1 Jan 2000` `1 Mar 2020` `1 Mar 2023` EQUALS `IN TIME`
-- Not yet commenced: today is the last day (edge), the day after, and months before.
#ASSERT `s 5 -- am I in time` `WA court` `another State` FALSE `1 Jan 2000` `1 Mar 2023` FALSE `1 Jan 2000` `1 Mar 2020` `1 Mar 2023` EQUALS `STILL IN TIME`
#ASSERT `s 5 -- am I in time` `WA court` `another State` FALSE `1 Jan 2000` `2 Mar 2023` FALSE `1 Jan 2000` `1 Mar 2020` `1 Mar 2023` EQUALS `OUT OF TIME`
#ASSERT `s 5 -- am I in time` `WA court` `another State` FALSE `1 Jan 2000` `7 Nov 2022` FALSE `1 Jan 2000` `1 Mar 2020` `1 Mar 2023` EQUALS `STILL IN TIME`
-- Across 29 February: time began 29 February 2024, last day 28 February 2027 (1095 days on); commenced on it and the day after.
#ASSERT `s 5 -- am I in time` `WA arbitrator` `a Territory` TRUE `28 Feb 2027` `7 Nov 2026` FALSE `1 Jan 2000` `29 Feb 2024` `28 Feb 2027` EQUALS `IN TIME`
#ASSERT `s 5 -- am I in time` `WA arbitrator` `a Territory` TRUE `1 Mar 2027` `7 Nov 2026` FALSE `1 Jan 2000` `29 Feb 2024` `28 Feb 2027` EQUALS `OUT OF TIME`
-- New Zealand law, declared: s 5 applies and the time is counted the same way.
#ASSERT `s 5 -- am I in time` `WA court` `NZ` TRUE `2 Mar 2023` `7 Nov 2026` TRUE `1 Jan 2000` `1 Mar 2020` `1 Mar 2023` EQUALS `OUT OF TIME`
-- Where s 5 does not apply, the encoding gives no time answer: WA law; outside WA; New Zealand undeclared; instituted before 1994.
#ASSERT `s 5 -- am I in time` `WA court` `WA law` TRUE `2 Mar 2023` `7 Nov 2026` FALSE `1 Jan 2000` `1 Mar 2020` `1 Mar 2023` EQUALS `NO TIME LIMIT FROM THIS ACT`
#ASSERT `s 5 -- am I in time` `outside WA` `another State` TRUE `2 Mar 2023` `7 Nov 2026` FALSE `1 Jan 2000` `1 Mar 2020` `1 Mar 2023` EQUALS `NO TIME LIMIT FROM THIS ACT`
#ASSERT `s 5 -- am I in time` `WA court` `NZ` TRUE `2 Mar 2023` `7 Nov 2026` FALSE `1 Jan 2000` `1 Mar 2020` `1 Mar 2023` EQUALS `NO TIME LIMIT FROM THIS ACT`
#ASSERT `s 5 -- am I in time` `WA court` `another State` TRUE `1 Jun 1993` `7 Nov 2026` FALSE `1 Jan 2000` `1 Mar 2020` `1 Mar 2023` EQUALS `NO TIME LIMIT FROM THIS ACT`

§ `s 6 -- how must the court use a discretion under that limitation law`

-- A WA court asked to extend time under another State's limitation law; following that State's courts is practicable.
#ASSERT `s 6 -- how must the court use a discretion under that limitation law` `WA court` `another State` TRUE `10 Jun 2020` `7 Nov 2026` FALSE `1 Jan 2000` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `FAVOUR`
#ASSERT `s 6 -- how must the court use a discretion under that limitation law` `WA court` `another State` TRUE `10 Jun 2020` `7 Nov 2026` FALSE `1 Jan 2000` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `NOT FAVOUR`
-- Not practicable (no comparable cases): s 6 says no more.
#ASSERT `s 6 -- how must the court use a discretion under that limitation law` `WA court` `another State` TRUE `10 Jun 2020` `7 Nov 2026` FALSE `1 Jan 2000` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `NOT PRACTICABLE`
#ASSERT `s 6 -- how must the court use a discretion under that limitation law` `WA court` `another State` TRUE `10 Jun 2020` `7 Nov 2026` FALSE `1 Jan 2000` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `NOT PRACTICABLE`
-- No discretion under that law, or none asked for.
#ASSERT `s 6 -- how must the court use a discretion under that limitation law` `WA court` `another State` TRUE `10 Jun 2020` `7 Nov 2026` FALSE `1 Jan 2000` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `NO DISCRETION`
-- An arbitrator in WA, a Territory's law, not yet commenced.
#ASSERT `s 6 -- how must the court use a discretion under that limitation law` `WA arbitrator` `a Territory` FALSE `10 Jun 2020` `7 Nov 2026` FALSE `1 Jan 2000` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `FAVOUR`
-- New Zealand declared, instituted after the declaration.
#ASSERT `s 6 -- how must the court use a discretion under that limitation law` `WA court` `NZ` TRUE `10 Jun 2020` `7 Nov 2026` TRUE `1 Jan 2000` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `NOT FAVOUR`
-- WA's own limitation law; a foreign country's; a court outside WA.
#ASSERT `s 6 -- how must the court use a discretion under that limitation law` `WA court` `WA law` TRUE `10 Jun 2020` `7 Nov 2026` FALSE `1 Jan 2000` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `S6 NOT WA OR NOT ANOTHER PLACE`
#ASSERT `s 6 -- how must the court use a discretion under that limitation law` `WA court` `a foreign country` TRUE `10 Jun 2020` `7 Nov 2026` FALSE `1 Jan 2000` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `S6 NOT WA OR NOT ANOTHER PLACE`
#ASSERT `s 6 -- how must the court use a discretion under that limitation law` `outside WA` `another State` TRUE `10 Jun 2020` `7 Nov 2026` FALSE `1 Jan 2000` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `S6 NOT WA OR NOT ANOTHER PLACE`
-- s 3 first: New Zealand undeclared; New Zealand instituted before the declaration; instituted before 1994.
#ASSERT `s 6 -- how must the court use a discretion under that limitation law` `WA court` `NZ` TRUE `10 Jun 2020` `7 Nov 2026` FALSE `1 Jan 2000` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `S6 NOT UNDER THIS ACT`
#ASSERT `s 6 -- how must the court use a discretion under that limitation law` `WA court` `NZ` TRUE `31 Dec 1999` `7 Nov 2026` TRUE `1 Jan 2000` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `S6 NOT UNDER THIS ACT`
#ASSERT `s 6 -- how must the court use a discretion under that limitation law` `outside WA` `WA law` TRUE `1 Jun 1993` `7 Nov 2026` FALSE `1 Jan 2000` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `S6 NOT UNDER THIS ACT`
